cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
title: "EvoMap: a browser-based open-source platform for geographic visualization of pathogen outbreak data in resource-constrained settings"
version: 0.1.0
date-released: "2026-04-01"
license: MIT
type: software
abstract: >-
  EvoMap is an open-source web application for geographic outbreak
  visualization, built to run entirely in the browser without
  server-side computation, API tokens, or environment configuration.
  v0.1.0 provides an interactive Leaflet map with automatic marker
  clustering, dataset search and filter controls, a responsive layout,
  and Docker support for institutional self-hosting. Phylogenetic tree
  visualization and live sequence-repository integration are
  architecturally scaffolded and targeted for v0.2.0 and v1.0.0
  respectively.
authors:
  - family-names: Adedeji
    given-names: John Adeyemo
    affiliation: Osun State University, Osogbo, Nigeria
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0009-0004-1257-4551"
repository-code: "https://github.com/Jonahnki/EvoMap"
url: "https://evomap-pqsmqim0i-john-adedejis-projects.vercel.app"
doi: 10.5281/zenodo.19362602
keywords:
  - pathogen outbreak visualization
  - geographic surveillance
  - web-based bioinformatics
  - public health informatics
  - low-resource settings
  - genomic epidemiology

